  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "For each integer \\(N\\gt1,\\) define positive integers to be congruent if they leave the same nonnegative remainder when divided by \\(N.\\) If \\(69,\\) \\(90,\\) and \\(125\\) are congruent in one such system, then in that same system, \\(81\\) is congruent to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(5\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(7\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(8\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "4"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1971-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The modulus \\(N\\) divides both \\(90-69=21\\) and \\(125-90=35.\\) Since \\(N\\gt1,\\) this forces \\(N=7.\\) Then \\(81\\equiv4\\pmod7.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The modulus divides the difference of any two congruent integers",
        "Use the differences \\(21\\) and \\(35\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
